# TRON Payments — C4 Architecture Guardrails

Canonical reference: **`docs/architecture.md`**. This rule is a session-level summary.

## C1 — Actors and External Systems

| Actor | Access |
|---|---|
| Finance Requester | Create payment requests |
| Signer | Review + sign with Ledger (WebHID) |
| Executor | Broadcast after threshold |
| Admin | Users, config, reference data |
| Auditor | Read-only audit access |

External: TRON Mainnet RPC, TronScan, Corporate OIDC (or email+password / Ledger login), Ledger hardware wallets, Let's Encrypt (production TLS).

## C2 — Containers

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  WEB[WebSPA_React_WebHID] --> NGINX[nginx_TLS]
  WEB -->|WebHID| LED[Ledger_USB]
  NGINX --> API[API_Fastify]
  API --> PG[(PostgreSQL)]
  API --> TRON[TRON_RPC]
```

| Container | Must stay |
|---|---|
| Web SPA | React + Vite; thin pages; WebHID Ledger in `src/ledger/`. Production image: nginx (SPA + `/api` reverse proxy, TLS). |
| API | Fastify; Drizzle; no signing capability; no Ledger access |
| PostgreSQL | Append-only audit; optimistic locking on requests |

**Forbidden:** backend Ledger access, private keys anywhere, arbitrary smart contract calls, raw tx upload via UI.

**Allowed:** browser WebHID Ledger access in the hosted SPA on user gesture only (secure context: HTTPS or localhost).

